course: dictionary
lesson: 12206
title: Congestion: too much in one place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Congestion means too many cars or people in one place, so things move slowly or get stuck. Think of a road at school-run time, when every car is trying to use it at once.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The motorway was full of congestion after the accident, and our bus took two hours to go a few miles.» Stuck traffic and a very slow bus show that congestion means a jam.
explain: Congestion can also describe a blocked nose or chest when you have a cold. «Mum gave me a tissue because my nose was full of congestion.» Check the clues: is the sentence about cars and people, or about a body that feels stuffed up?
explain: Congestion is a noun, and the adjective is congested. «The congested road made us late for school.» Congested means full and blocked.
fact: Congestion means too many cars or people in one place, so movement is slow.
fact: Traffic congestion is when roads are too full of vehicles to move freely.
fact: Congestion can also mean a blocked feeling in the nose or chest from a cold.
fact: «Congestion» is a noun; the adjective is «congested».
fact: Some cities, such as London, have a congestion charge: drivers pay to enter the busy centre.
exercise: «The motorway was full of congestion after the accident.» What does congestion mean here? | A loud noise from a radio | *Too many cars, so the traffic moves very slowly | Clean, fresh air on a sunny day | A large, empty car park
exercise: Mia has a cold and says, «My nose is full of congestion.» What does she mean? | She can smell very well | Her nose is too big for her face | *A blocked nose, with too much mucus | She has a cold in her ears
exercise: Which word in «The congested road made us late for school.» means full and blocked? | late | road | *congested | made
test: «The city centre had heavy congestion at lunchtime, so the bus crawled along.» What does congestion mean? | Rain falling hard | A new bus route | *Too many cars and people, so movement is slow | An empty road with no cars
test: Dad says, «Your congestion will clear up in a few days, so drink lots of water.» What is the congestion? | *A blocked nose or chest from a cold | A traffic jam on the motorway | A new kind of bus | A school trip
exam: «Councils try to cut traffic congestion by building cycle lanes, and London's congestion charge makes drivers think twice.» What does traffic congestion mean in this sentence? | A quiet, empty street | A blocked nose from a cold | *Too many vehicles on the roads, so movement is slow | A new kind of bicycle
